sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch12-57> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-57--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-57--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch12-57: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.30" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.305"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/mixed" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.5"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The conditional limit is the emulation argument already available for universal cellular automata: a system that can emulate its predictor cannot be systematically outrun. The sentence applies that limit to science as such, which requires the systems science studies, or the universe, to be irreducible in this strong sense. Nothing now public establishes that physical hypothesis, and a run of successful predictions leaves a claim about everything undecided." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: If the dynamics under study are a universal computation, no predictor that is itself an effective process computes every consequence faster than the system produces them. A universality proof discharges that conditional for systems such as rule 110. An explicit shortcut for all consequences of our universe's rules would refute the application to science, and no such pair of rules and shortcut is in hand." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "A claim that science never predicts everything has no finite observational cutoff.", "The outrunning argument applies to universal systems, and whether the universe is one is open.", "Success on reducible questions is compatible with a permanent limit and with the absence of one." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch12-57--grok--dataset-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-57--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of wolfram2002-ch12-57 by Grok 4.7: 0.4" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.4"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-57--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch12-57> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-57--grok--operationalizability> .
